**Definition 1.2 (source, action and observation).** Let

$$
\mathcal T::=\alpha\mid\beta\mid\langle\mathcal T,\mathcal T\rangle,
\qquad
\operatorname{ht}(\alpha)=\operatorname{ht}(\beta)=0,
\qquad
\operatorname{ht}\langle u,v\rangle=1+\max(\operatorname{ht}u,\operatorname{ht}v).
$$

Pairing is free and ordered. Every finite original-root word in $L,R$,
including the empty word, is a legal literal Read. Its reply $r_T(a)$ is
alpha or beta at a leaf, branch at a pair, and absent after traversal
passes a leaf. The reply alphabet, substitution and source family are
exactly

$$
\begin{aligned}
\mathcal A&=\{\alpha,\beta,\mathsf{branch},\mathsf{absent}\},\\
\rho\alpha&=\beta,\qquad \rho\beta=\langle\beta,\alpha\rangle,\qquad
\rho\langle u,v\rangle=\langle\rho u,\rho v\rangle,\\
\mathcal F_D&=\{\langle\alpha,v\rangle:\operatorname{ht}(v)\le D\},
\qquad D\ge1,\\
W_D&=\{q:|q|\le D-1\},\qquad \mathcal P_D=\{Rq:q\in W_D\}.
\end{aligned}
\tag{OCC.1}
$$

There is one stationary actual initial source throughout preparation and
late acquisition. The expression $\rho^kT$ is a prediction target, not
an update performed during that acquisition.

